simpled - a simple init that reads systemd units
================================================
simpled is PID 1 for miviex. It reads a subset of systemd's unit files
and does what matters of systemd's work: targets, dependencies and
ordering, restarts, clean stops with timeouts, and the shutdown. It is
a single-threaded loop of a few hundred lines more than it has features.

simplectl starts, stops and inspects units, enables and masks them, and
is poweroff, reboot and halt when called by those names.


Units
-----
Units are searched in /etc/simpled/system, then PREFIX/lib/simpled/system.
Services and targets are supported, templates (getty@.service started as
getty@tty1.service) and aliases (default.target -> multi-user.target).

[Unit]     Description Wants Requires After Before Conflicts
           StartLimitBurst StartLimitIntervalSec
[Service]  Type=simple|oneshot RemainAfterExit ExecStartPre ExecStart
           ExecStop ExecReload Restart=no|on-failure|always RestartSec
           TimeoutStopSec KillSignal User Group WorkingDirectory UMask
           Environment EnvironmentFile StandardInput=null|tty
           StandardOutput StandardError=journal|console|tty|null|inherit
           TTYPath
[Install]  WantedBy

Specifiers: %n %N %p %i %I %%. A '-' before a command ignores its exit
status. Unknown keys are reported with file and line, and skipped.

Each service runs in its own session; stopping it signals its process
group. Output goes to /var/log/simpled/<unit>.log ("journal").


Control
-------
miviex has no Unix sockets yet: simplectl writes a request file to
/run/simpled/req and sends SIGUSR1, which only root can do. start, stop
and restart wait for their jobs and report failures (--no-block does
not wait). simpled keeps each unit's state in /run/simpled/units/<unit>,
so status, is-active and list work for every user without a request.

Signals to simpled: SIGTERM, SIGINT (Ctrl+Alt+Del) reboot, SIGUSR2
powers off, SIGHUP rereads unit files.


Building
--------
Edit config.mk and config.h (copied from config.def.h), then:

	make
	make check     # runs simpled unprivileged, and as PID 1 in a namespace
	make install

For miviex: make CC=musl-gcc LDFLAGS="-static -s"
